    "Set rater pay per task or hourly, with rate differentiated by task complexity and required expertise; track pay against throughput to catch quality-degrading speed incentives.",
    "Rotate task types and cap session length to reduce rater fatigue, which is a known driver of annotation-quality decay on long sessions.",
    "Aggregate comparisons into a preference dataset (chosen/rejected response pairs) and feed it into reward-model training or direct preference optimization (DPO).",
    "Periodically audit vendor-reported quality metrics against an independent gold-standard set rather than relying solely on vendor-supplied QA numbers.",
